# Tape-to-Cloud — Free-Tier Self-Sustaining Improvement Loop

16 modules: audit, analytics, vtl-cloud, restore, disk-ingest, email-extract, email-migrate, tape-duplicate, media-ingest, tape-ops, tape-saas, tape-vault, destroy, llm-corpus, ml-enrich, monetize.

Every change: **discover → evaluate → integrate → verify → release**. Free tier only — no paid SaaS, no Bugbot, no Max Mode, no Ollama/GPU.

## Model routing (95/5)

**Bucket A (95%):** Grok Code Fast 1 → Grok 4.5 → GPT-5.6 Luna → Claude Haiku 4.5

**Bucket B (5%):** Composer 2.5 Standard — vendor format readers, Snowball/Tape Gateway, WORM/NIST 800-88, Temporal restore-at-scale, Nexus chain-of-custody

**Bucket C (≤1%, user-request only):** Sonnet 5, Opus 5, Fable 5.1

## Hard rules

1. **No Bugbot.** CI replacement: `prek` + Ruff + zizmor + OSV-Scanner + actionlint. Cap hit → Ruff locally + CI on PR; do not retry Bugbot.
2. **No paid Cursor features** (Background Agents, Bugbot Pro, Max Mode).
3. Before done: `uv run ruff check --fix .`, `uv run ruff format .`, `uv run prek run --all-files`, `uv run pytest -q`.
4. SHA-pin every new GitHub Action: `uses: owner/action@<sha>  # vX.Y.Z`.
5. Conventional Commits; CHANGELOG from commits.
6. **`uv` only** for Python deps (`uv add`, `uv lock`, `uv sync`, `uv run`).
7. One PR = one concern.
8. Free-tier only: OSV.dev, Dependabot, Renovate, GlitchTip/SigNoz self-host when needed — not Snyk/Sentry cloud/Bugbot Pro.

## Pre/post session commands

```bash
git pull --rebase origin main && uv sync --all-groups && uv run prek run --all-files && uv run pytest -q
# ... work ...
uv run ruff check --fix . && uv run ruff format . && uv run prek run --all-files && uv run pytest -q
```

## Monday 9 AM AEST (15–90 min)

1. Dependabot dashboard PRs
2. Renovate Dependency Dashboard — approve batched minor/patch
3. Security tab — OSV/Dependabot alerts
4. Model feed watcher logs — bump pins if needed
5. Track Awesome List RSS — eval queue candidates
6. Latest release / CHANGELOG accuracy
7. `discovery/tape-to-cloud/free-tool-inventory.md` — new loop-internal or module-library candidates

